TradeLens Engineering Workflow
1. Purpose
This document defines the standard workflow for implementing, testing, committing, pushing, reviewing, and merging TradeLens engineering stories.
The objective is to ensure:
•	No work is lost between Cursor, local development and GitHub. 
•	Every story has a clearly identifiable baseline. 
•	Branches and commits are unambiguous. 
•	Changes are independently verifiable. 
•	Regression testing is performed before merge. 
•	Product development can proceed without requiring the Product Owner to understand Git internals. 
 
2. Roles
Product Owner
Defines:
•	What should be built 
•	Why it is required 
•	Product priorities 
•	Acceptance criteria 
Cursor / Development Agent
Responsible for:
•	Implementation 
•	Unit/integration tests 
•	Code changes 
•	Commit creation 
•	Reporting exact Git state 
Technical Checkpoint
Before any merge, verify:
•	Branch 
•	Baseline 
•	Commit 
•	Changed files 
•	Tests 
•	Remote branch 
•	PR status 
•	Working tree 
________________________________________
3. Golden Rule
Never treat an agent's statement that something is "committed" or "complete" as proof that the change exists in Git.
Git itself is the source of truth.
A commit is considered verified only when:
git cat-file -t <SHA>
returns:
commit
A change is considered safely preserved only when the commit also exists on the remote branch.
