5. Baseline Verification
Before starting a story:
git status
git branch --show-current
git log --oneline -1
The Product Owner should not proceed if:
•	The wrong branch is checked out. 
•	There are unexpected local changes. 
•	The baseline commit is unclear. 
The baseline must be explicitly recorded in the Cursor implementation prompt.
Example:
BASELINE
Branch: main
Commit: b9c1ae0
Working tree: clean
________________________________________
6. Branching
Each story gets a dedicated branch.
Example:
cursor/er-0025-launch-ux
The branch must be created from the agreed baseline.
Do not:
•	Reset 
•	Rebase 
•	Cherry-pick 
•	Merge another development branch 
unless explicitly instructed.
________________________________________
7. Cursor Implementation Prompt
Every substantial implementation prompt should contain:
Scope
What is being built.
Acceptance criteria
What must work.
Files allowed to change
Explicitly identified.
Files that must not change
Especially:
•	Recommendation Engine 
•	Mentor Engine 
•	API contracts 
•	dependencies 
•	unrelated frontend/backend modules 
unless required by the story.
Testing requirements
Exact tests to run.
Git safety
GIT SAFETY
- Work only on the specified branch.
- Do not switch branches.
- Do not reset, rebase, cherry-pick or merge.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Do not change dependencies unless explicitly required.
- Do not push unless instructed.
- Report the exact commit SHA.
- Report git status after implementation.
________________________________________
8. Commit Verification
After Cursor commits:
git status
git log --oneline --decorate -5
git cat-file -t <COMMIT_SHA>
Expected:
commit
Also verify the commit contents:
git show --stat --oneline <COMMIT_SHA>
________________________________________
9. Push Verification
Push only after tests and commit verification:
git push origin HEAD
Then:
git status
git branch -vv
The remote branch must be confirmed.
A commit is not considered safely preserved merely because Cursor says it was pushed.
________________________________________
10. Pull Request
The PR should identify:
•	ER/story number 
•	Baseline 
•	Commit SHA 
•	Scope 
•	Tests 
•	Known pre-existing failures 
•	Out-of-scope changes 
Before merge, verify the actual PR diff rather than relying solely on the agent's summary.
________________________________________
11. Regression Gate
Every story must define its regression suite.
For TradeLens, the minimum relevant areas generally include:
•	Single Source of Truth / recommendation authority 
•	Stock detail recommendation 
•	Market data abstraction 
•	Candidate screening 
•	Opportunity ranking 
•	Relevant frontend tests 
•	API tests where applicable 
Known pre-existing failures must be explicitly documented and never silently classified as new failures.
________________________________________
12. Worktrees
Worktrees are allowed and useful, but their purpose must always be explicit.
Example:
TradeLens/
TradeLens-er0022/
Before using a worktree:
git worktree list
Never assume that a branch exists in every worktree.
If a commit exists in Cursor but not locally, first:
git fetch origin --prune
Then verify the remote branch.
________________________________________
13. Four Git States
We will use these terms consistently:
State	Meaning
Implemented	Cursor says the code is complete
Committed	Git commit exists and SHA is verified
Pushed	Commit exists on GitHub
Merged	Commit is part of main
Only the last three are Git-verifiable.
 
14. Product Owner Safety Rules
The Product Owner should not execute:
git reset
git rebase
git cherry-pick
git merge
git push --force
git clean
unless explicitly instructed.
When a command could potentially affect existing work, the Product Owner should stop and provide the command output before proceeding.
 
15. Definition of Done
An ER/story is considered complete only when:
•	Correct baseline confirmed 
•	Dedicated branch created 
•	Implementation completed 
•	Scope reviewed 
•	Tests pass 
•	Known failures documented 
•	Commit SHA verified 
•	Working tree clean 
•	Remote branch verified 
•	PR created 
•	CI passes 
•	PR reviewed 
•	PR merged 
•	main verified 
•	New baseline SHA recorded

